OL,3,CMan jailed for keeping mother's body
OL,4,Cin freezer for nearly three years
OL,6,FA man has been jailed after keeping
OL,7,Fhis dead mother in a freezer for
OL,8,Fnearly three years whilst claiming
OL,9,Fbenefits.
OL,11,FChristopher Phillips has been
OL,12,Fsentenced to two years and four months
OL,13,Fin prison.
OL,15,FChristopher Phillips, 60, of
OL,16,FPorthcawl, previously pleaded guilty
OL,17,Fto preventing the lawful and decent
OL,18,Fburial of a dead body, and to fraud by
OL,19,Ffalse representation.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G1/4
